#%RAML 1.0 DataType
(package): Project
type: string
displayName: ProductCatalogModel
description: |
  Determines how Product Variants are managed in the Project.
(enumDescriptions):
  Classic: |
    Product Variants are embedded in the Product. This is the default model.
  InMigration: |
    This temporary model supports migration from `Classic` to `Modular`. Product Variants remain embedded, and Product API Variant update actions remain supported. Other resources that resolve Variants default to standalone Variants, while Product Search defaults to embedded Variants. See the [migration guide](/guides/migration-guides/modular-catalog-migration) for details.
  Modular: |
    Product Variants are standalone resources managed through the [Variants API](/projects/variants). Pricing uses [StandalonePrices](ctp:api:type:StandalonePrice). Embedded Prices and Product API Variant update actions are unsupported.
    - Variant-related update actions on Products return a `400` error.
    - Products must be created without `masterVariant` and `variants`.
    - Products cannot be deleted while Variants reference them.
    - Products cannot be unpublished while they have published Variants.
    - [Carts](/projects/carts) read variant data from the Variant API instead of embedded Product Variants.
    - `priceMode` on Products is set to `Standalone`.
enum:
  - Classic
  - InMigration
  - Modular
